# NPC aggro link groups (aggro_links / npc_aggro_links), data-inferred rule AGGROLINK-1.
#
# Members of group 70: NPC 8219 "Sichimi bandit fighter" (helper, aggro_link_help_dist 50) and
# NPC 8220 "Sichimi bandit ruffian" (leader, also group 72). main_world places them together at
# (24201.326, 8912.35, 567) and (24198.924, 8906.95, 567). Both templates are non-aggressive
# with `aggro_link_special_rule_id` 0, so neither helps the other through the template rules
# (`UpdateAggroHelp` needs `aggression` for rule 0). With the link group, 8219 must join when
# 8220 is attacked.
#
# The world spawner jitters placements (and the roaming AI walks them apart), so spawn one copy
# of each next to the bot; the bot spawn point is 10.8 km from any main_world 8219/8220
# placement, so `nearest` cannot pick a world copy. The helper distance of 50 m absorbs the
# drift of the two roaming spawns. GM access is needed for `/spawn npc`; the game log must run
# with `aaemu_game::systems::ai::behaviors=debug` (`Scripts/verify.sh` sets it).
suite aggro-links
bot linker gm

[linker]
gm spawn npc 8219
pump 1
gm spawn npc 8220
pump 1
units 8219 8220
castraw 2 8220
expectlog "aggro link: group member joined the fight" 20
pump 4
